Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Revised from the 67%-accuracy strategy with one targeted diagnosis in mind:
// the main failure was not arithmetic validity inside spans, but *missing or
// delayed opening of spans* because unconstrained generation had to literally
// sample the token "<<". That caused many answers to contain no valid <<...>>
// computations at all, or to open too late after lots of prose.
//
// Targeted changes:
// 1. Outside constrained mode, we now use short unconstrained chunks and
//    proactively open a constrained span as soon as the recent unconstrained
//    suffix looks like a natural place for a computation: after "=", "is",
//    "are", "was", "were", "be", "gives", "get", "gets", "got", "total",
//    "sum", "difference", "product", "quotient", "so", "thus", "then", "now",
//    "therefore", "answer", "Answer", or after punctuation like ":" "." ",".
//    This removes reliance on the LM sampling "<<", which was the key observed
//    bottleneck.
// 2. We still penalize raw ">>" outside spans and mildly discourage "<<"
//    during unconstrained chunking, so accidental delimiter corruption remains
//    unlikely.
// 3. Inside constrained mode, we keep the successful design choice from the
//    best prior strategy: immediate close whenever the parser says the span is
//    complete, plus parser-masked constrained sampling with strong boosts for
//    caller-supplied arithmetic token groups and a strong penalty on nested
//    "<<". This preserves syntax while encouraging short arithmetic snippets.
// 4. Recovery for overlong spans is retained but made simpler: roll back to a
//    boundary token "(" and spend one step on recovery, then let the next
//    iteration either close or continue from the repaired prefix.
// 5. We also open a span immediately if the unconstrained sampler itself emits
//    "<<", preserving compatibility with models that already know the desired
//    format.
//
// Overall, this is still a delimiter-based CSD, but now delimiter *entry* is
// largely strategy-controlled rather than left to chance, directly addressing
// the evaluation failures while keeping the previously verified constrained
// arithmetic behavior.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In unconstrained-chunk branches we remain outside, so the
//   implication is vacuous; if we proactively open a span, OpenConstrainedSpan
//   sets currentConstrainedOut := [], which is parser-valid by precondition.
//   In the close branch we leave constrained mode, so the implication is again
//   vacuous. In the recovery branch, RollbackToBoundary returns a parser-valid
//   repaired prefix which we assign to currentConstrainedOut. In the manual
//   constrained-sampling branch, ConstrainedSample guarantees EOS or a token
//   valid after currentConstrainedOut, and AppendConstrainedToken preserves
//   parser validity.
// suffix: Outside constrained mode the implication is vacuous; when we open a
//   span, currentConstrainedOut becomes [], which is the empty suffix of the
//   new generated ending in "<<". In the close branch we leave constrained
//   mode, so the suffix invariant is vacuous. In the recovery branch, repaired
//   is a prefix of the old constrained content, and trimming exactly the
//   dropped suffix from generated preserves that the end of generated equals
//   repaired. In the constrained append branch, AppendConstrainedToken appends
//   the same token to generated and currentConstrainedOut, preserving the
//   suffix relationship.
// cost accounting: We return cost := steps. The unconstrained-chunk branch uses
//   UnconstrainedChunk and increments steps by the returned stepsUsed; if it
//   then proactively opens a span, OpenConstrainedSpan costs internally and we
//   also spend one more loop step via steps := steps + 1. The close branch uses
//   CloseConstrainedSpan and increments steps by 1. The recovery branch is
//   query-only, so it explicitly increments steps by 1. The constrained manual
//   branch uses ConstrainedSample, then either breaks on EOS or appends one
//   token and increments steps by 1. Thus every non-breaking branch advances
//   steps consistently and cost := steps satisfies cost <= maxSteps.
// progress: UnconstrainedChunk appends exactly stepsUsed tokens, so after
//   steps := steps + stepsUsed the bound |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| +
//   steps is preserved; if we then open a span, generated grows by 1 and steps
//   also grows by 1. The close branch appends at most one token and increments
//   steps by 1. The recovery branch shrinks or preserves generated while still
//   incrementing steps by 1. The constrained append branch appends exactly one
//   token and increments steps by 1, while EOS breaks immediately. Therefore
//   the progress bound is preserved in every branch.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var steps: nat := 0;
var flatGroups := helpers.FlattenTokenGroups(validTokenGroups);

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> generated[|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|..] == currentConstrainedOut
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  invariant cost == 0
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if !insideConstrainedOut {
    var remaining := maxSteps - steps;
    var chunkCap: nat := 1;
    if remaining >= 3 {
      chunkCap := 2;
    }
    var chunkGenerated, stoppedOnOpenSpan, stoppedOnEos, stepsUsed := helpers.UnconstrainedChunk(
      lm, prompt, generated, chunkCap, "<<", eosToken
    );
    generated := chunkGenerated;
    steps := steps + stepsUsed;

    if stoppedOnEos {
      break;
    } else {
      if stoppedOnOpenSpan {
        insideConstrainedOut := true;
        currentConstrainedOut := [];
      } else {
        if steps < maxSteps && "<<" in lm.Tokens {
          var prevTok, foundPrev := helpers.LastTokenBefore(generated, " ");
          var shouldOpen := false;
          if |generated| == 0 {
            shouldOpen := false;
          } else {
            var last := generated[|generated| - 1];
            if last == "=" || last == ":" || last == "." || last == "," {
              shouldOpen := true;
            } else {
